## Self-curation — every session before I sign off

The Reflexion + A-MEM + Generative-Agents triad. **Do all of these. Not optional.**

1. **Importance-scored writes.** Anything appended to `memory/what-works.md`,
   `memory/decisions.md`, or `memory/failures.md` carries an entry-level
   frontmatter block:
   ```yaml
   importance: 1-10   # rate at moment of capture
   captured: YYYY-MM-DD
   tags: [...]
   ```
   Higher importance = stronger eviction protection during the next dream pass.
2. **Failure attribution** (Reflexion). If something didn't work, append to
   `memory/failures.md` with an explicit *why* — not just "didn't land." Failure
   notes move the needle more than success notes.
3. **Cross-link on write** (A-MEM Zettelkasten). When you append a new entry,
   scan the file for entries that contradict, refine, or supersede it. **Edit
   those entries** — add a `superseded_by: [[new-entry-slug]]` line, or refine
   their content. Append-only without revision creates drift.
4. **Two-Output Rule.** Every meaningful Q→A also mutates a durable page in the
   host project. If you answered something useful, write the conclusion to the
   relevant doc/notes file, not just to the chat. Synthesis must compound.
5. **Chronology line.** Append one line to `log.md`:
   `## [YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM] kind | one-line title`
6. **Task hygiene.** Did you close anything? Mark `done <date>` in
   `tasks/open-tasks.md`. New commitment? Add it with `📅` + `⏫` priority.
7. **MEMORY.md budget check.** Tier 2 must stay ≤80 lines. If you grew it,
   trim now — move detail into `memory/INDEX.md` or topic files.

## Surfacing my own backlog

At session start, after reading `tasks/open-tasks.md`: surface anything
**overdue or due-this-week** before doing other work. Don't bury it.

